 "title": "مشكلة الباص  (Trouble on the Bus)",
 "level": "A1 — beginner",
 "labels": {
  "layan": "ليان",
  "mariam": "مريم",
  "faten": "مس فاتن"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Moments after that calm morning, popular student Layan blocks Mariam from riding the school bus, and soon Principal Ms. Faten calls Mariam into her office over a false report. Listen to the whole exchange in Jordanian Arabic first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "قلت للسائق هدول البنات مش معنا عالباص.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "ليش بتحكي هيك يا ليان؟",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "يلا، انزلي من الباص هلأ.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "ليش دايماً بتحكموا فينا هيك؟",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "عاملين حالهم عصابة بالمدرسة.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "بس مش بعد اليوم.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "بعرف إنك هربتي من الباص اليوم.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "لا يا مس فاتن، هاد الحكي مش صح.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "مين حكى إلك هاد الإشي؟",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "البنات عم بكذبوا عليكي.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "زميلتك بالصف حكت إلي كل إشي.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "وهاد الموضوع لفت انتباهي.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go back through the scene and unpack each line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "قلت للسائق هدول البنات مش معنا عالباص.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I told the driver these girls are not with us on the bus.' Layan uses ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "هدول",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " for \"these\" when talking about people, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "عالباص",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " fuses \"on\" and \"the bus\" into one smooth spoken word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "ليش بتحكي هيك يا ليان؟",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why are you talking like that, Layan?' In Jordanian Arabic, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "ليش",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"why\"—shortened from \"for what thing\"—and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "هيك",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"like that\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "يلا، انزلي من الباص هلأ.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Come on, get off the bus right now.' Notice ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "layan",
   "t": "هلأ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the everyday Amman word for \"now\", squeezed down from the longer phrase \"this hour\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "ليش دايماً بتحكموا فينا هيك؟",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why do you always boss us around like this?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "دايماً",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"always\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "بتحكموا فينا",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally says \"you rule in us\", a vivid way to say someone bosses you around.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "عاملين حالهم عصابة بالمدرسة.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'They act like a gang at school.' The handy expression ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "عاملين حالهم",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally means \"making themselves\", which is how Jordanians say people are acting like big shots.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "بس مش بعد اليوم.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'But not after today.' Short and punchy: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "بس",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"but\" or \"only\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "مش",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the everyday spoken word for \"not\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "بعرف إنك هربتي من الباص اليوم.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I know that you skipped the bus today.' Ms. Faten says ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "هربتي",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", built from the root for running away, which school staff use when a student skips class or the bus.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "لا يا مس فاتن، هاد الحكي مش صح.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, Ms. Faten, this talk is not true.' Here ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "الحكي",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"the talk\" or \"what people are saying\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "مش صح",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the quickest way to say \"not true\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "مين حكى إلك هاد الإشي؟",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Who told you this thing?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "مين",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " asks \"who\" in Levantine Arabic, while ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "حكى",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the everyday word for \"spoke\" or \"told\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "البنات عم بكذبوا عليكي.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The girls are lying to you.' Putting the tiny word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "عم",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " before ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "mariam",
   "t": "بكذبوا",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " works just like English \"-ing\", showing they are lying right now.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "زميلتك بالصف حكت إلي كل إشي.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Your classmate told me everything.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "زميلتك",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means \"your female classmate\", with ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "ك",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " tacked onto the end to mean \"your\" when speaking to a girl.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "وهاد الموضوع لفت انتباهي.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And this matter caught my attention.' Word for word, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "faten",
   "t": "لفت انتباهي",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " says \"it turned my attention\", a polished phrase Ms. Faten uses in formal school moments. Now listen to the whole scene again at natural speed.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
